1. What is Amazon S3?
Writing

“Amazon S3 is an object storage service used to store and retrieve unlimited data with high durability, scalability, and availability.”

✅ 2. What is an S3 bucket?
Writing

“An S3 bucket is a container that stores objects like files and metadata in S3.”

✅ 3. What is S3 durability and availability?
Writing

“S3 provides 99.999999999% durability by storing data redundantly across multiple Availability Zones.”

✅ 4. What are S3 storage classes?
Writing

“S3 storage classes optimize cost and performance, such as Standard, Intelligent-Tiering, Standard-IA, Glacier, and Deep Archive.”

✅ 5. What is versioning in S3?
Writing

“Versioning keeps multiple versions of an object, helping recover from accidental deletion or overwrite.”

✅ 6. How do you secure an S3 bucket?
Writing

“We secure S3 using IAM policies, bucket policies, encryption, and blocking public access.”

✅ 7. What is an S3 lifecycle policy?
Writing

“Lifecycle policies automatically move objects to cheaper storage classes or delete them to reduce cost.”

✅ 8. What is S3 replication?
Writing

“S3 replication automatically copies objects to another bucket in the same or different region for backup or disaster recovery.”

✅ 9. Difference between S3 and EBS?
Writing

“S3 is object storage accessed via API, while EBS is block storage attached to EC2 instances.”

✅ 10. What is S3 encryption?
Writing

“S3 supports encryption at rest using SSE-S3, SSE-KMS, and encryption in transit using HTTPS.”

